issues.body:
#### Technical Details

Phase 2 runs the buffer refill and the inactive-LP drain in the same body call ([L748-L753](https://github.com/Lynxify-xyz/lynx-contracts/blob/0082743/hardhat/contracts/LynxKeeperRouter.sol#L748-L753)):

```solidity
bool refilled = refillBuffer();
bool drained = reconcileInactiveLp();
if (drained) _pullLpRecoveredWhbar();
```

`refillBuffer()` pulls staking principal into the vault's idle buffer. `reconcileInactiveLp()` then calls `lpAllocator.drainPosition()`, and `_pullLpRecoveredWhbar()` calls `manager.pull()`, both without a `try/catch`. A revert in either one unwinds the whole `executeWeeklyOpsBody()` call, including the refill that already succeeded. [`_runWeeklyOpsBodyBestEffort()`](https://github.com/Lynxify-xyz/lynx-contracts/blob/0082743/hardhat/contracts/LynxKeeperRouter.sol#L591-L608) catches the failure and emits `WeeklyOpsBodyFailed`, and the router moves on to phase 3. The buffer is therefore not refilled until the next cycle.

The drain is market-sensitive:

- [`_decreaseDisabledPosition()`](https://github.com/Lynxify-xyz/lynx-contracts/blob/0082743/hardhat/contracts/LynxLpAllocator.sol#L1126-L1140) prices its minimums through `_trustedSqrtPriceX96()`. That call reverts when the TWAP is unavailable or spot deviates from it by more than `maxSpotDeviationBps`, and the NPM then checks the TWAP-priced minimums against spot.
- The full-balance swap fails as described in #5.
- `manager.pull()` reverts `ImpairmentValuationFailed` when the LP strategy cannot be valued.

When the failure persists, as with the donation in #5, the refill is lost every week.

A broader version of this issue, filed against the single-call weekly body during the previous fix review (yAudit/linxify-report#35), was closed without changes. The phase split in this delta isolates the other stages but leaves the refill and the drain in one call.

#### Impact

Low. A drain failure in phase 2 costs the vault that week's buffer refill. Redemptions beyond the remaining idle WHBAR are then delayed even though staking principal is available. A persistent failure suppresses the refill every week. No funds are lost, and the router owner can call `refillBuffer()` directly.

#### Recommendation

Isolate the drain and the recovery pull from the refill. For example, catch the drain inside `reconcileInactiveLp()` and the pull inside `_pullLpRecoveredWhbar()`, emitting a failure event:

```diff
-            lpAllocator.drainPosition(sn, deadline);
-            emit InactiveLpDrained(sn);
-            return true;
+            try lpAllocator.drainPosition(sn, deadline) {
+                emit InactiveLpDrained(sn);
+                return true;
+            } catch (bytes memory err) {
+                emit InactiveLpDrainFailed(sn, err);
+                return false;
+            }
```

Alternatively, run the refill in its own phase.

#### Developer Response

Fixed in commits [79d4d3d](https://github.com/Lynxify-xyz/lynx-contracts/commit/79d4d3d21621fc81987352432f27777b6848a8ad), [619c5ee](https://github.com/Lynxify-xyz/lynx-contracts/commit/619c5eeab47b4e4ad460eba2df021578b03cdaac), together with #19. The drain now runs in its own phase.
